<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shadegan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fallahiyeh, Fallahiyah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shadegan, formerly Fallahiyeh, is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khuzestan">Khuzestan</a> province in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, near the large Shadegan wetlands at the head of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a>. In the 18th century it became the seat of the sheikhs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-kab">Banu Ka'b</a>, an Arab tribe that controlled the marshes and the date and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> lands of lower Khuzestan. It was renamed Shadegan in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-persian">Pahlavi</a> period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shadegan.jpg" alt="Shadegan" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Seyed Khalil Mousavi · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shadegan_International_Wetlands_(12).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
